{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448954-narrative-dissonance","id":1448954,"title":"Narrative Dissonance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-19T02:16:02-07:00","id":1448954,"title":"Narrative Dissonance","content":"I have almost finished reading my recently arrived physical copy of Cults (love it). I have come again across this odd phenomenon. I wanted to ask you whether you also got this impression and maybe have a better name for it. <br /> <br /> 1. <b>So world of darkness works like a like dark reflection. But it does not only look like it. It has a different logic to the real world, an emotional logic.</b><br /> <br /> The worst of what you feel the real world works like is true in this story world.<br /> <br /> Conspiracy theorists that think the world is run by a shadowy cabal are surprisingly common. It <i>feels </i>logical.<br /> - I would argue that in the real world this is mostly misguided or even dangerous.<br /> - In the world of darkness this is actually true and useful <br /> <br /> 2. <b>This principle of emotional logic is broken in many places - to me.</b><br /> <br /> - The beckoning. The old and powerful are called away to never be heard of again (so far). <br /> The powerful become more powerful and the poor become poorer.<br /> <br /> - The Sabbat are called away never to be heard of again (so far). <br /> A more violent factions takes over and comes to your home.<br /> <br /> - The big fat corporate HQ in Vienna gets blown up splintering the organisation<br /> Some desperate fools turn terrorist and try to blow HQ up. The powers that be go on a rampage and create more desperate fools.<br /> <br /> - The world was fairly secular but religion is coming back.<br /> The world was religious, but it is becoming secular. People feel empty and turn towards new causes. <br /> <br /> - Splintered family that hates and kills itself comes together (though still dysfunctional and with the occasional dead family member.)<br /> Everyone is 100% only pretending. Murder and theft snowball leading to sure implosion.<br /> <br /> <b>I am looking in this case through the lense of <i>emotional </i>logic, not real logic or narrative usefulness. </b><br /> <br /> Is there any usefulness to this perspective? <br /> Do you have a better name than Emotional Narrative Dissonance? (Not counting hate, edition war or whining ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T02:52:16-07:00","id":1448956,"title":"","content":"i think there are 2 flaws with your logic 1 it's a game, some desissions are made for the sake of game design.<br /> <br /> secondly (and let's channel that inner malk for a sec): you're thinking to small, in the eternal game of the jyhad there's always a bigger player and they will destroy vampiric society and the stability and safety it gave you if it serves their incomprehensible purrposes, disapearance of elders and the sabbath, just a bunch of pawns being moved to where they're needed, the vienna chantry, just a rook being sacrificed. the methusulas or the antedeluvians themselves are making moves that are so obviously seen means that something big is about to go down. the hecatta is a bunch of former enemies coming together because they can all see the shit flying towards the fan and they hope that they can use the others as shields in the upcoming shitshow, leaving them the sole survivors.<br /> <br /> and the influx of cults is anything but good. these cults that give divine purpose to ones vanity and thirst for power, that promote sin and suffering or have their goal be nothing more then the utter annialation of thounsands of lives if not existence itself<br /> <br /> if anybody sees these points you've made, these signs that things are comming to an end, these exploitations of the desire for a purpose in life and unlife, as a force for good, then they're either blind or utterly mad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T03:13:29-07:00","id":1448957,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25992\" data-vbnamecard=\"25992\">archderd</a> Thank you for your reply.<br /> 1. If you are making a game play vs narrative decision. I am not suggesting that it is wrong. This needs to be playable. But if it is a trade of there is a cost.<br /> 2. There is always a bigger fish - yes.<br /> 3. I do not think the cults are good in the world of darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T03:32:00-07:00","id":1448958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mfalkenb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448954-narrative-dissonance?p=1448957#post1448957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25992\" data-vbnamecard=\"25992\">archderd</a> Thank you for your reply.<br /> 1. If you are making a game play vs narrative decision. I am not suggesting that it is wrong. This needs to be playable. But if it is a trade of there is a cost.<br /> 2. There is always a bigger fish - yes.<br /> 3. I do not think the cults are good in the world of darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>it's a cost most ppl expect any game to pay and it's something you'll always need to consider when discussing game lore.<br /> and what i tried to illustrate is that under emotional logic or conspiracy logic or whatever you want to call it the things you call broken isn't, that little speech is meant to be like the rant of a raving conspiracy theorist too prove said point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T04:08:39-07:00","id":1448960,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't really agree with half of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mfalkenb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448954-narrative-dissonance#post1448954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The beckoning. The old and powerful are called away to never be heard of again (so far).<br /> The powerful become more powerful and the poor become poorer.</div> </div> </div> </div>The old and powerful also <i>die.</i> When Alexander the Great conquered everything there was to conquer, he didn't create an eternal ultra-rich empire of awesome. He died and his empire splintered and it all went to shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mfalkenb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448954-narrative-dissonance#post1448954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The Sabbat are called away never to be heard of again (so far).<br /> A more violent factions takes over and comes to your home.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean. Sometimes? But anyway, Sabbat was never an internal extremist faction. They've always been an external enemy gnawing at the borders of the Camarilla. And then they lost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mfalkenb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448954-narrative-dissonance#post1448954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The big fat corporate HQ in Vienna gets blown up splintering the organisation<br /> Some desperate fools turn terrorist and try to blow HQ up. The powers that be go on a rampage and create more desperate fools.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally don't like the way Vienna chantry was handled, but there's a lesson there. <i>Vampires are not powers that be.</i> They are parasites who keep existing at the sufferance of mankind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mfalkenb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448954-narrative-dissonance#post1448954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- The world was fairly secular but religion is coming back.<br /> The world was religious, but it is becoming secular. People feel empty and turn towards new causes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mfalkenb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448954-narrative-dissonance#post1448954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Splintered family that hates and kills itself comes together (though still dysfunctional and with the occasional dead family member.)<br /> Everyone is 100% only pretending. Murder and theft snowball leading to sure implosion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hecata are weird and jamming them into a single &quot;family&quot; was weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T04:31:33-07:00","id":1448961,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Kammerer;n1448960]Yeah, I don't really agree with half of this.<br /> <br /> <br /> The old and powerful also <i>die.</i> When Alexander the Great conquered everything there was to conquer, he didn't create an eternal ultra-rich empire of awesome. He died and his empire splintered and it all went to shit. /QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I can live very well with say 33% for an exploratory idea.<br /> <br /> Alexander is a good real world example. I do not think WOD generally follows this logic. When was the last time the big bad just dropped dead? No epic struggle, no bigger fish, no surprise escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T04:39:12-07:00","id":1448962,"title":"","content":"There's a certain reverse logic actually. I live in Kentucky where there actually are cabals of people who deny health care to the public, actively cooperate with corporations to flood the state with drugs, and are immense religious hypocrites belonging to extremists doomsday sects that wield tremendous power.<br /> <br /> It's just these are the Far Right.<br /> <br /> It's just instead of Mitch McConnell, the conspiracy theorists of my state blame Jews and liberals. I feel it's the same in the WOD. The Ultra-Rich and corrupt are vampires but people blame the innocent.<br /> <br /> Qanon isn't any more right in the WOD but are useful fools for making fear about money and power (as well as magic) sound ludicrous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-19-2021, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T11:25:06-07:00","id":1449016,"title":"","content":"Shadowy cabals and &quot;the Deep state&quot; are ideas favoured by crazed conspiracy theoriests, but shadowy cabals and the &quot;deep state&quot; aren't pure fiction. Let's imagine your city's public transport sucks because of the influence of some wealthy people want you to depend more on cars and buy more fuel so they can line their pockets. That actually happens in America. Is that not the work of a cabal? Is that not the &quot;deep state&quot;. Some people have very poor interpretations of very reasonable ideas. <br /> <br /> But yes, the part where V5 cuts down on the power gap, when in reality that power gap is deepening, is really a good bit of cognitive dissonance. That part where goverments go after the people in the wrong, rather than siding with them to benefit from their resources, is a good bit of cognitive dissonance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T11:48:42-07:00","id":1449021,"title":"","content":"&quot;Deep State&quot; talk is mostly a misinterpretation of what would more accurately be called a Hybrid-Regime.<br /> I would call the most accurate term for the American system a Hybrid-Regime.<br /> <br /> The four pillars of this Hybrid-Regime are combination of corporate control over the media, first-past-the-post elections, gerrymandering, and Citizens United.<br /> <br /> Corporate control over the media allows those corporations to manufacture consent for economically rightwing policies by framing all issues from an economically rightwing perspective, and starving those disaproved of by corporations of coverage.<br /> <br /> First Past the Post elections prevent the rise of 3rd parties in response to corruption. Voting for a 3rd party in such a system effectively elects your worst opposition, which dis-incentivizes people from even trying, and blocks such parties from ever reaching a critical mass. This means that once corporations have corrupted the two main parties, that corruption is effectively eternal, as it can not cause the collapse of the party that would happen in a parliamentary system. Parties in a parliamentary system can easily collapse if they become corrupt, as people have many options that do not result in their biggest enemies gaining power.<br /> <br /> Gerrymandering allows politicians to pick their voters rather than voters picking their politicians, gradually resulting in one-party states. This means that corporations only need to corrupt one party in many states. It also means that young politicians are more beholden to party leadership than to the people. This creates a Master/Apprentice relationship between young and old politicians, rather like the Sith. In such a system, networking older politicians and donors is far more important than creating policies that appeal to the people.<br /> <br /> Citizens United legalizes bribery, making politicians more beholden to those who have bribed them than to the people.<br /> <br /> Any two of these would result in what is officially called a Flawed Democracy. Four of them together moves America firmly into the Hybrid-Regime category.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T12:40:28-07:00","id":1449029,"title":"","content":"Conspiracy theorists ruin everything.<br /> <br /> Noam Chomsky gets cited in the GUIDE TO THE TECHNOCRACY but other people think that the Union are just another Right Wing theory about globalism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T18:14:20-07:00","id":1449066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mfalkenb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448954-narrative-dissonance?p=1448961#post1448961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alexander is a good real world example. I do not think WOD generally follows this logic. When was the last time the big bad just dropped dead? No epic struggle, no bigger fish, no surprise escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>zapathasura the ravnos antediluvian might be a good example. He's confirmed to be dead","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T18:56:20-07:00","id":1449074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mfalkenb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1448954-narrative-dissonance?p=1448961#post1448961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alexander is a good real world example. I do not think WOD generally follows this logic. When was the last time the big bad just dropped dead? No epic struggle, no bigger fish, no surprise escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm one of the people who believe he was poisoned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T01:03:54-07:00","id":1449232,"title":"","content":"For my V20 game, I made two big decisions at the outset regarding the nature of the setting: <br /> 1.) While elements of Mage Lore apply, there are no &quot;True&quot; Mages or Ascension War behind the scenes of this setting. I feel that Mage's &quot;Battle for Reality&quot; tagline takes a bit too much oomph from the other splats and reduces them to spinoffs of the &quot;real&quot; conflict of the World of Darkness.<br /> 2.) Vampires <i>influence</i> society at almost every level but directly control very little. Fear of backlash from a reorganized Inquisition (whether from organized religion or secular authorities) discourages such activities. Ghouling a billionaire or top political, military bureaucrats etc. is not countenanced by Elders who have the greatest stake in the status quo. It would be comforting to lay the sins of history and everything else wrong with the world at the feet of immortal monsters, but in truth humans need no manipulation to establish corrupt systems of control which the Kindred are happy to use. In our increasingly connected, populist times top-down manipulation of society is harder than ever, even as younger Kindred use the fragmented forms of mass media to cultivate herds and carve out little fiefdoms of influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}